Vendored Lua 5.4.9 (library only)
====================================

Source: https://www.lua.org/ftp/lua-5.4.9.tar.gz
License: MIT (see lua.org/license.html — the sources carry no separate
LICENSE file; the MIT terms are stated on lua.org and in doc/readme.html
of the upstream tarball).

Contents: the full src/*.c + src/*.h library set, EXCLUDING the two
standalone mains lua.c and luac.c (interpreter/compiler frontends we
never build — nalar only embeds the library).

Why vendored: hooks embed Lua on every target (Linux/macOS/Windows).
System Lua lives in different places per OS (or nowhere), so compiling
from source removes all probing. Built with -std=c99 -O2 and NO
platform -D defines: the core language + the stdlib subset hooks need
is define-free. (Dynamic C-module loading via require() is unavailable;
hooks are plain scripts and never need it.)
